# Rapport d'Architecture — ImmoSync AI

## 1. Setup & Stack Technique

- Frontend: React.js (Vite), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Zustand, SPA
- Backend: Python, FastAPI, architecture hexagonale (API / Services / Repositories)
- BDD: PostgreSQL, SQLAlchemy, Alembic
- Authentification: JWT, rôles `agent`, `manager`
- IA: OpenAI API
- Stockage fichiers: AWS S3
- Déploiement/DevOps: Docker, Docker Compose, GitHub Actions, Nginx, AWS ECS, CloudFront, AWS RDS PostgreSQL

---

## 2. Schéma Relationnel de la Base de Données

### Entités principales

- `Agency`
- `User`
- `Property`
- `PropertyImage`
- `Buyer`
- `BuyerCriteria`
- `Match`
- `Visit`
- `Offer`
- `Contract`
- `Alert`
- `BuyerStageHistory`

### Tables

- `agencies`
  - `id` PK
  - `name`
  - `created_at`

- `users`
  - `id` PK
  - `agency_id` FK -> `agencies.id`
  - `email`
  - `password_hash`
  - `role`
  - `created_at`

- `properties`
  - `id` PK
  - `agency_id` FK -> `agencies.id`
  - `title`
  - `address`
  - `city`
  - `postal_code`
  - `price`
  - `surface_m2`
  - `rooms`
  - `bedrooms`
  - `has_garden`
  - `dpe_rating`
  - `status`
  - `description`
  - `created_at`
  - `updated_at`

- `property_images`
  - `id` PK
  - `property_id` FK -> `properties.id`
  - `s3_key`
  - `url`
  - `alt`
  - `created_at`

- `buyers`
  - `id` PK
  - `agency_id` FK -> `agencies.id`
  - `created_by` FK -> `users.id`
  - `first_name`
  - `last_name`
  - `email`
  - `phone`
  - `stage`
  - `notes`
  - `created_at`
  - `updated_at`

- `buyer_criteria`
  - `id` PK
  - `buyer_id` FK -> `buyers.id`
  - `min_price`
  - `max_price`
  - `min_surface_m2`
  - `max_surface_m2`
  - `min_rooms`
  - `min_bedrooms`
  - `required_garden`
  - `max_dpe_rating`
  - `city`
  - `raw_criteria_text`
  - `updated_at`

- `matches`
  - `id` PK
  - `buyer_id` FK -> `buyers.id`
  - `property_id` FK -> `properties.id`
  - `score`
  - `reason`
  - `status`
  - `created_at`

- `visits`
  - `id` PK
  - `buyer_id` FK -> `buyers.id`
  - `property_id` FK -> `properties.id`
  - `scheduled_at`
  - `status`
  - `notes`
  - `created_at`

- `offers`
  - `id` PK
  - `buyer_id` FK -> `buyers.id`
  - `property_id` FK -> `properties.id`
  - `amount`
  - `status`
  - `submitted_at`
  - `created_at`

- `contracts`
  - `id` PK
  - `buyer_id` FK -> `buyers.id`
  - `property_id` FK -> `properties.id`
  - `signed_at`
  - `status`
  - `created_at`

- `alerts`
  - `id` PK
  - `agency_id` FK -> `agencies.id`
  - `buyer_id` FK nullable -> `buyers.id`
  - `property_id` FK nullable -> `properties.id`
  - `type`
  - `message`
  - `created_at`
  - `read_at`

- `buyer_stage_history`
  - `id` PK
  - `buyer_id` FK -> `buyers.id`
  - `from_stage`
  - `to_stage`
  - `changed_by` FK -> `users.id`
  - `changed_at`

### Relations

- `agencies` 1-N `users` via `users.agency_id`
- `agencies` 1-N `properties` via `properties.agency_id`
- `agencies` 1-N `buyers` via `buyers.agency_id`
- `agencies` 1-N `alerts` via `alerts.agency_id`
- `users` 1-N `buyers` via `buyers.created_by`
- `users` 1-N `buyer_stage_history` via `buyer_stage_history.changed_by`
- `properties` 1-N `property_images` via `property_images.property_id`
- `buyers` 1-1 `buyer_criteria` via `buyer_criteria.buyer_id`
- `buyers` N-N `properties` via `matches`
- `buyers` N-N `properties` via `visits`
- `buyers` N-N `properties` via `offers`
- `buyers` N-N `properties` via `contracts`
- `buyers` 1-N `alerts` via `alerts.buyer_id`
- `properties` 1-N `alerts` via `alerts.property_id`
- `buyers` 1-N `buyer_stage_history` via `buyer_stage_history.buyer_id`

